      "writtenOn": "2022-06-29T18:25:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "help me understand why we embed the profile information in the mime/mediatype\nfor these, yet for things like AAC audio, the profile information handled separately.\n\nthis feels like it leads to having many separate\nif (its DTSHD_PROFILE1 || DTSHD_PROFILE2 || ....) { ...}\ninstead of\nif (its DTSHD) {  and we handle profiles within the DTSHD specific code }\n\nthis puts the profile determination into the DTSHD codecs.\nas written, if we want to add a DTSHD_PROFILE3, we have to modify the framework.\n\nI\u0027m in agreement with the MIMETYPE_AUDIO_VND_DTSHD, but i\u0027m questioning the 4 entries that have PROFILE in their name.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21472,
